    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d105">

                <pb facs="0147" n="135" sameAs="frus:frus1943v02/pg135"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to
                        the Governor General of French West Africa</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Boisson</hi>)<anchor n="44"
                        xml:id="d105-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-06-04">June 4, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Governor General</hi>: I have made choice of
                    Admiral William Glassford as my Personal Representative in French West Africa,
                    to reside at Dakar with the rank of Minister.</p>
                <p>Admiral Glassford, a distinguished Naval officer of long experience, has been
                    selected for this important mission because of his outstanding ability and high
                    character; and he is fully apprised of the mutual interests and problems of our
                    two Governments. I commend him to Your Excellency.</p>
                <p>Very sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Franklin D. Roosevelt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
